{"operations":[{"content":"The quorum of the general assembly is one third of the members present, as established by the amendment adopted 2 May 2026. Where the amendment of 2 May 2026 and the bylaws differ, the amendment applies.\n\n[[cite:obs-447b19c5077175503ca3f636b6a991d2b7fc29de \"Section Quorum is amended: the general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present.\"]]\n[[cite:obs-27eefa4f0015d54641c7a69ba8c699bb324b115f \"The general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present.\"]]","expected_sha256":"436a15c7e332c0d188ca4600961246fbd84f9499c7fef4c72f7d8c338d24b363","kind":"modify","path":"doc/quorum.md"}],"rationale":"Added the quorum definition from the amendment of 2 May 2026, and stated that the amendment overrides the bylaws where they differ, with exact citations from both sources."}